1
00:00:10,930 --> 00:00:15,930
Hello and welcome to this module on risk mitigation.

2
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:20,930
In this module, we will be discussing the application of the five controls,

3
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:25,930
which are elimination, substitution, engineering controls,

4
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:29,930
administrative controls, and personal protective equipment,

5
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:33,930
which can be applied in conjunction with each other

6
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:39,930
to reduce the risks posed by operations involving biological agents.

7
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:46,100
I am now at a Biosafety Level 3 facility,

8
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:51,100
which is designated as a BSL-3 facility.

9
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:55,100
This is essentially a containment zone

10
00:00:55,100 --> 00:01:00,100
in which researchers and laboratory workers

11
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:03,100
can work with biological agents

12
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,100
and conduct research in an environment

13
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:11,100
which limits the risk posed by these biological agents.

14
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:18,460
There are two types of containment,

15
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:22,460
primary containment and secondary containment.

16
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:26,460
Primary containment pertains to the protection

17
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:30,460
of the laboratory user from the biological agent

18
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:33,460
by the application of pertinent controls,

19
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:38,460
such as personal protective equipment and administrative controls.

20
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:42,460
Secondary containment, on the other hand,

21
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:46,460
pertains to the protection of the environment

22
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,460
from the biological agent

23
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:53,460
by the application of appropriate engineering controls

24
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:57,460
and standard operating procedures.

25
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:00,460
Both primary and secondary containment

26
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,460
can be applied in conjunction with each other

27
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:09,460
to limit the risk of exposure to biological agents.

28
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,460
This module, which follows,

29
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:16,460
will focus on the application of pertinent controls

30
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:22,460
to mitigate or limit the risk posed by biological agents.

31
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:26,460
We will now proceed to the slide presentation.
